    {
      "id": 44152,
      "name": "Matchstickman",
      "username": "Matchstickman",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/matchstickman/{size}/1880_2.png",
      "created_at": "2012-11-12T11:32:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>1)The Kraken will target villains</p><p>2)That depends. 2 Krakens would be 2 seperate 5 point damaging cards, not a single 10 point attack but 2 Cramped Quarters Combat (Megalopolis environment) would both add 1 damage for a total of +2 for any damage! The reason being that you process the cards one at a time but if they have 'global' effects then the effects stick around until the card disappears.</p><p>3) No. If a single line is on a card says something like \"Deal up to 3 targets 3 melee damage\" (a single effect) or \" Deal 1 target 2 melee damage and a second target 3 projectile damage\" (specifies a second target) then it needs to be separate targets. If a card has multiple lines that say something like \"Invincible Jones deals a target 2 lightning damage. Invincible Jones deals a target 2 infernal damage\" then it can be the same target as a) it doesn't specify a second/different target, and b) it is two separate effects.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>... and I think that's the last time I'll be using Paul's Invincible Jones example as we now have a 'proper' hero who has a card with that effect on it, Invincible Jones I salute you and all the fine work you have done, you would have made a fine promo deck</p>",
      "post_number": 2,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:17:43.902Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
