      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>1)The Kraken will target villains</p><p>2)That depends. 2 Krakens would be 2 seperate 5 point damaging cards, not a single 10 point attack but 2 Cramped Quarters Combat (Megalopolis environment) would both add 1 damage for a total of +2 for any damage! The reason being that you process the cards one at a time but if they have &#39;global&#39; effects then the effects stick around until the card disappears.</p><p>3) No. If a single line is on a card says something like &quot;Deal up to 3 targets 3 melee damage&quot; (a single effect) or &quot; Deal 1 target 2 melee damage and a second target 3 projectile damage&quot; (specifies a second target) then it needs to be separate targets. If a card has multiple lines that say something like &quot;Invincible Jones deals a target 2 lightning damage. Invincible Jones deals a target 2 infernal damage&quot; then it can be the same target as a) it doesn&#39;t specify a second/different target, and b) it is two separate effects.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>... and I think that&#39;s the last time I&#39;ll be using Paul&#39;s Invincible Jones example as we now have a &#39;proper&#39; hero who has a card with that effect on it, Invincible Jones I salute you and all the fine work you have done, you would have made a fine promo deck</p>",
